 "level_notes": {
  "1": "XML DTDs are defined inside the W3C XML 1.0 Recommendation (Fifth Edition, 2008) — there is no separate DTD specification. The SGML original, ISO 8879:1986, is paywalled.",
  "0": "Every validating XML parser implements DTDs: libxml2 (valid.c), Apache Xerces (XMLDTDScannerImpl), and expat (non-validating, but parses the internal subset and entities). The W3C XML Conformance Test Suite covers DTD validity.",
  "3": "Entity expansion is the root of the 'billion laughs' denial-of-service attack; see the Wikipedia entry."
 },
